    <statement><p>Simplify each expression as much as possible
and leave it without radicals.</p>
<p>(a) <m>\sqrt{ w^{4} x^{8} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>\sqrt[3]{ 125 w^{6} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) <m>\sqrt{25 x^{6} y^{2} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>(d) <m>\sqrt{ 18 w^{5} y^{8} } \sqrt{ 2 y^{8} w^{3} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>w^{2}x^{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5w^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5x^{3}y^{1}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6w^{4}y^{8}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> SOLUTION </alert>



(a) <m>\sqrt{ w^{4} x^{8} } = (w^{4} x^{8})^{1/2} =
       w^{4/2} x^{8/2} = w^{2}x^{4}</m>.



(b) <m>\sqrt[3]{ 125 w^{6} } = (125 w^{6})^{1/3} = 125^{1/3} w^{6/3} =
       5w^{2}</m>.



(c) <m>\sqrt{25 x^{6} y^{2} } = (25 x^{6} y^{2})^{1/2} =
       5x^{3}y^{1}</m>.



(d) <m>\sqrt{ 18 w^{5} y^{8} } \sqrt{ 2 y^{8} w^{3} } =
       \sqrt{ (18 w^{5} y^{8})\cdot (2 y^{8} w^{3}) } =
       ( 36 w^{8} y^{16} )^{1/2} =
       6w^{4}y^{8}</m>.



</solution>
